meta {
  name: Get Quote Recap (Edit View)
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/quote-recaps/{{createdQuoteRecapId}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

script:post-response {
  // Captured so `Update Quote Recap` can prove the patch did not move it.
  bru.setVar("quoteRecapQuoteDate", res.getBody().quoteDate);
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("carries the lead context, so the form needs one request", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body).to.have.property("context");
    expect(body.context).to.have.property("leadId");
    expect(body.context).to.have.property("primaryContactName");
    expect(body.context).to.have.property("householdAddress");
    expect(body.context.householdId).to.equal(bru.getVar("quoteContextHouseholdId"));
  });

  test("round-trips sameAsHousehold — the reason this endpoint exists", function () {
    // `Create Quote Recap` sends `sameAsHousehold: true` on the Home row and
    // omits it on the Auto row. Without this the edit form cannot restore the
    // toggle to the position the producer left it in.
    const policies = res.getBody().policies;
    expect(policies).to.have.lengthOf(2);
    expect(policies[0].sameAsHousehold).to.equal(false);
    expect(policies[1].sameAsHousehold).to.equal(true);
  });

  test("returns the attached document as metadata", function () {
    const document = res.getBody().document;
    expect(document.filename).to.equal("carrier-quote.pdf");
    expect(document.contentType).to.equal("application/pdf");
    expect(document).to.have.property("size");
    expect(document).to.have.property("uploadedAt");
  });

  test("round-trips the renewal month (PAC-56 #16)", function () {
    // What `Create Quote Recap` sent. The form seeds the select from this, so a
    // recap edited for an unrelated reason must not lose it.
    expect(res.getBody().insuranceRenewalMonth).to.equal("March");
  });

  test("returns the totals as they stand before the edit", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.premium).to.be.a("number");
    expect(body.itemCount).to.be.a("number");
    expect(body.productsQuoted).to.be.an("array");
  });

  test("never leaks internals", function () {
    const raw = JSON.stringify(res.getBody());
    expect(raw).to.not.contain("agencies/");
    expect(raw).to.not.contain("submissionToken");
    expect(raw).to.not.contain("isTestRecord");
    expect(res.getBody().document).to.not.have.property("key");
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /quote-recaps/:id — the edit form's payload (PAC-56 #11)

  Everything `/quote-recaps/:id/edit` needs to render, in **one** round trip.

  - **Module:** `quote_recaps`
  - **Permission:** `quote_recaps:read` (class-level; the PATCH adds `:write`)
  - **Data scope:** `own` — another producer's recap **404s**, never 403s.

  ## Why the lead context is embedded

  The edit route is keyed by **recap id**. Fetching the context separately would
  mean first learning the recap's `leadId` and then issuing a second request —
  a waterfall on a page that cannot paint until both have landed. So this
  returns `context` byte-identical to `GET /quote-recaps/context?leadId=`, and
  the page mounts the same `LeadContextHeader` and feeds the same
  `householdAddress` to the "same as household address" toggle.

  ## Why `sameAsHousehold` is here and not on `GET /leads/:id`

  The Lead Detail contract deliberately exposes only the **resolved** address: a
  row the producer ticked "same as household" stores a *copy* of the household
  address, not a flag for the reader to re-interpret. That is right for
  rendering and useless for editing, where the toggle has to come back up in the
  position it was left. So the flag lives on this endpoint alone.

  ## Response

  ```json
  {
    "id": "…",
    "context": {
      "leadId": "…", "primaryContactName": "Dana Ruiz",
      "householdId": "…", "householdName": "Ruiz Household",
      "householdAddress": { "street": "…", "city": "…", "state": "…", "zip": "…" },
      "leadStatus": "Quoted"
    },
    "policies": [
      { "policyType": "Auto", "premium": 1180, "itemCount": 2,
        "propertyAddress": null, "sameAsHousehold": false },
      { "policyType": "Home", "premium": 940, "itemCount": 1,
        "propertyAddress": { … }, "sameAsHousehold": true }
    ],
    "insuranceRenewalMonth": "March",
    "notes": "…",
    "document": { "filename": "carrier-quote.pdf", "contentType": "application/pdf",
                  "size": 12345, "uploadedAt": "…" },
    "quoteDate": "…", "status": "Submitted",
    "premium": 2120, "itemCount": 3, "productsQuoted": ["Auto", "Home"],
    "legacyPropertyAddress": null
  }
  ```

  `document.key` is never returned — opening the file goes through
  `GET /quote-recaps/:id/document/download`.

  `legacyPropertyAddress` is the recap-level dwelling that only pre-PAC-56-#14
  recaps carry. Read-only: the form has no field for it, and saving migrates the
  recap to per-row addresses.

  `insuranceRenewalMonth` (PAC-56 #16) is `null` on every migrated recap and on
  anything recorded before the field existed. The form treats that as **unset**,
  not invalid — its edit schema accepts `""` where the create schema does not,
  because rejecting it would lock every migrated recap out of editing. Values
  are normalized on read, so a recap holding SmartSuite's choice UUID still
  comes back as a month name.

  ## Errors
  - `404` — malformed id, unknown recap, another agency's, or out of data scope.
    All four are deliberately indistinguishable.
  - `400` — the recap is not linked to a lead (only reachable on unmigrated data;
    `GET /leads/:id` self-heals the link).

  ## Run order
  Depends on `createdQuoteRecapId` from **Create Quote Recap** (seq 4).
}
